er\u202fFarrelly’s 2019 Best‑Picture win) and generic presenter shots (Shia\u202fLaBeouf, etc.), confirming that the video is **a montage of multiple ceremonies** rather than the full, chronological flow of a single event.  \n- Throughout, the setting remains a formal auditorium with a stage, red curtains, golden lighting, and an audience in tuxedos and gowns; the ABC broadcast logo appears repeatedly, but no on‑screen year or “92nd Academy Awards” graphic is visible.  \n- No musical performances or backstage footage are captured in the selected frames.\n\n**Conclusion** – The visual evidence tracks several key Oscar personalities across the clip, showing isolated award‑acceptance and presentation moments from both the 2019 and 2020 ceremonies. Because the footage is a compilation and lacks the opening, closing, musical numbers, and continuous backstage context, the claim that the video “narrates the complete process of the 2020 Oscars ceremony” is **incorrect**.', 'failed_images': []}

